BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION This model uses [`x`] as the number of years since 2000. So for the year 2010, [`x`] is [`10\text{:}`]
[```\newcommand{\substitute}[1]{{\color{blue}{{#1}}}}\newcommand{\amp}{&} \begin{aligned} 620+32.35(\substitute{10})\amp = 943.50 \end{aligned} ```]
