END_LATEX_IMAGE
############################################################ # Body ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML The height inside a tent when you are [`d`] feet from the west wall of the tent is given by the formula [`\newcommand{\abs}[1]{\left\lvert#1\right\rvert}h=-2\abs{d-3}+6\text{,}`] where [`h`] is in feet.
>> [@image(insertGraph($image_1), width=>282, alt=>qq"an A-frame tent with guidelines indicating that d feet inward from one side, the height to the ceiling at that point is d feet")@]* <<
END_PGML
############################################################ # Scaffold ############################################################ Scaffold::Begin(numbered => 1,is_open => "correct_or_first_incorrect",can_open => always,);
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML When you are [`5`][$NBSP]*ft from the west side, the height is [_]{$height1}{10}.
END_PGML
############################################################ # Solution ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION When [`d=5\text{,}`] we have:
[```\newcommand{\abs}[1]{\left\lvert#1\right\rvert}\newcommand{\substitute}[1]{{\color{blue}{{#1}}}}\newcommand{\amp}{&} \begin{aligned} h\amp= -2\abs{d-3}+6\\ h\amp= -2\abs{\substitute{5}-3}+6\amp\amp\text{Review order of operations in }\text{Section A.5}\text{.}\\ \amp= -2\abs{2}+6\amp\amp\text{Review absolute value in }\text{Section A.3}\text{.}\\ \amp= -2(2)+6\\ \amp= -4+6=2 \end{aligned} ```]
So when you are [`5`][$NBSP]*ft from the west side, the height of the tent is [`2`][$NBSP]*ft.
END_PGML_SOLUTION
Section::End();
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML When you are [`2.5`][$NBSP]*ft from the west side, the height is [_]{$height2}{10}.
END_PGML
############################################################ # Solution ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION When [`d=2.5\text{,}`] we have:
[```\newcommand{\abs}[1]{\left\lvert#1\right\rvert}\newcommand{\substitute}[1]{{\color{blue}{{#1}}}}\newcommand{\amp}{&} \begin{aligned} h\amp= -2\abs{d-3}+6\\ h\amp= -2\abs{\substitute{2.5}-3}+6\\ \amp= -2\abs{-0.5}+6\\ \amp= -2(0.5)+6\\ \amp=-1+6=5 \end{aligned} ```]
So when you are [`2.5`][$NBSP]*ft from the west side, the height of the tent is [`5`][$NBSP]*ft.
END_PGML_SOLUTION
Section::End();
Scaffold::End();
