############################################################ # PG Setup Code ############################################################ Context("Form"); Context()->variables->are(A=>'Real',B=>'Real',C=>'Real'); $ans = Formula("7/2 A + 4/3 B + 83/68 C"); $image_1 = createLaTeXImage(); $image_1->addToPreamble(latexImagePreamble()); $image_1->BEGIN_LATEX_IMAGE \begin{tikzpicture} \draw[fill=wood] (0,0) -- node[pos=0.5,below]{\(\frac{3}{2}A\)} (3,0) -- node[pos=0.5,below right]{\(\frac{2}{3}B\)} (5,1) -- node[pos=0.5,above right]{\(\frac{3}{4}C\)} (4,3) -- node[pos=0.5,above]{\(2A\)} (0,3) -- node[pos=0.5,above left]{\(\frac{2}{3}B\)} (-1,1) -- node[pos=0.5,below left]{\(\frac{8}{17}C\)} cycle; \end{tikzpicture}
END_LATEX_IMAGE
############################################################ # Body ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML Find the perimeter of this shape, which is not drawn to scale. Simplify the perimeter expression as much as possible.
>> [@image(insertGraph($image_1), width=>282, alt=>qq"a six-sided shape whose sides are labeled 3/2 A, 2/3 B, 3/4 C, 2A, 2/3 B, and 8/17 C")@]* <<
[_]{$ans}{20}
END_PGML
############################################################ # Solution ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION The perimeter is the result from adding the six sides together: [`\frac{3}{2}A+\frac{2}{3}B+\frac{3}{4}C+2A+\frac{2}{3}B+\frac{8}{17}C\text{.}`] There are two [`A`]-terms, two [`B`]-terms, and two [`C`]-terms. We need to find:
[```\newcommand{\amp}{&} \begin{aligned} \frac{3}{2}+2\amp=\frac{3}{2}+\frac{2}{1}\cdot\frac{2}{2} \amp\qquad\frac{2}{3}+\frac{2}{3}\amp=\frac{4}{3} \amp\qquad\frac{3}{4}+\frac{8}{17}\amp=\frac{3}{4}\cdot\frac{17}{17}+\frac{8}{17}\frac{4}{4}\\ \amp=\frac{3}{2}+\frac{4}{2} \amp\amp \amp\amp=\frac{51}{68}+\frac{32}{68}\\ \amp=\frac{7}{2} \amp\amp \amp\amp=\frac{83}{68} \end{aligned} ```]
So the perimeter is [`\frac{7}{2}A+\frac{4}{3}B+\frac{83}{68}C\text{.}`]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
