BEGIN_PGML You bought a new car for [`[$bc]`] with a zero interest loan over a five-year period. That means you'll have to pay [`[$rc]`] each month for the next five years ([`60`] months) to pay it off. According to this information, the equation [`y=[$f]`] models the loan balance after [`x`] months, where [`y`] is in dollars. Make a graph of this equation.
[_]{$gt}{1}
END_PGML
############################################################ # Hint ############################################################ #Set value of $showHint in PGcourse.pl for course-wide attempt threshhold for revealing hints
BEGIN_PGML_HINT Two relevant [`x`]-values to use are [`0`] and [`60\text{.}`] (Why?)
END_PGML_HINT
############################################################ # Solution ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION Time [`x`] is measured in months, and this loan will take [`60`] months to pay off. So we will make a table where the [`x`]-values run from [`0`] to [`60\text{.}`]
[# [. [@DataTable([[[PGML('[`x`]'),rowbottom=>'3',midrule=>'1',],PGML('[`y=[$f]`]'),],[PGML('[`0`]'),PGML('[`[$y[0]]`]'),],[PGML('[`15`]'),PGML('[`[$y[1]]`]'),],[PGML('[`30`]'),PGML('[`[$y[2]]`]'),],[PGML('[`45`]'),PGML('[`[$y[3]]`]'),],[PGML('[`60`]'),PGML('[`[$y[4]]`]'),],],align=>'cc',valign=>'middle', );@]* .] [. [@image(insertGraph($image_1), width=>240)@]* .]* #]*{align => 'p{40%}p{57%}',}
END_PGML_SOLUTION
