BEGIN_PGML
To make fuel for an automobile, you could mix [`x`] cubic meters of gasoline with [`y`] cubic meters of ethanol. The density of gasoline is [$A] kg per cubic meter, and the density of ethanol is [$B] kg per cubic meter. If you want to mix these types of fuel together to make a total of [$C] kg, write a linear equation in standard form that models the amounts of gasoline and ethanol you could mix.

[_]{$evaluator}{16}

END_PGML

############################################################
# End Problem
############################################################

ENDDOCUMENT();

