TEXT(beginproblem());

############################################################
# PG Setup Code
############################################################
Context('Numeric');
@x = random_subset(2,1..9);
@p = (Point(@x), -Point(@x), Point($x[0], -$x[1]), Point($x[1], -$x[0]));
@p = random_subset(4, @p);
for (0..3) {
  $ans[$_] = 'I'   if (($p[$_]->value)[0] > 0 && ($p[$_]->value)[1] > 0);
  $ans[$_] = 'II'  if (($p[$_]->value)[0] < 0 && ($p[$_]->value)[1] > 0);
  $ans[$_] = 'III' if (($p[$_]->value)[0] < 0 && ($p[$_]->value)[1] < 0);
  $ans[$_] = 'IV'  if (($p[$_]->value)[0] > 0 && ($p[$_]->value)[1] < 0);
  $d[$_] = DropDown(['I','II','III','IV'], $ans[$_], showInStatic => 0);
  $xposneg[$_] = (($p[$_]->value)[0] > 0) ? 'positive' : 'negative';
  $yposneg[$_] = (($p[$_]->value)[1] > 0) ? 'positive' : 'negative';
}
%qwords = (
  I => 'upper right',
  II => 'upper left',
  III => 'lower left',
  IV => 'lower right',
);
@ul = map {$qwords{$_}} @ans;

############################################################
# Body
############################################################

BEGIN_PGML
a.  [`[$p[0]]`] [_]{$d[0]}{5}

a.  [`[$p[1]]`] [_]{$d[1]}{5}

a.  [`[$p[2]]`] [_]{$d[2]}{5}

a.  [`[$p[3]]`] [_]{$d[3]}{5}

END_PGML

############################################################
# Solution
############################################################

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
a.  The [`x`]-coordinate is [$xposneg[0]] and the [`y`]-coordinate is [$yposneg[0]], so the point is in the [$ul[0]] quadrant, which is Quadrant [$ans[0]].

a.  The [`x`]-coordinate is [$xposneg[1]] and the [`y`]-coordinate is [$yposneg[1]], so the point is in the [$ul[1]] quadrant, which is Quadrant [$ans[1]].

a.  The [`x`]-coordinate is [$xposneg[2]] and the [`y`]-coordinate is [$yposneg[2]], so the point is in the [$ul[2]] quadrant, which is Quadrant [$ans[2]].

a.  The [`x`]-coordinate is [$xposneg[3]] and the [`y`]-coordinate is [$yposneg[3]], so the point is in the [$ul[3]] quadrant, which is Quadrant [$ans[3]].

END_PGML_SOLUTION

