############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML The number of people in a math class that play the ukulele.
This number is best considered as a [_]{$whole}{5}.
END_PGML
############################################################ # Solution ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION The number of people who play the ukulele could be [`0,1,2,\dots\text{,}`] so the whole numbers are the appropriate set.
END_PGML_SOLUTION
Section::End();
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML The hypotenuse's length in a given right triangle.
This number is best considered as a [_]{$real}{5}.
END_PGML
############################################################ # Solution ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION A hypotenuse's length could be [`1\text{,}`] [`1.2\text{,}`] [`\sqrt{2}`] (which is irrational), or any other positive number. So the real numbers are the appropriate set.
END_PGML_SOLUTION
Section::End();
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML The proportion of people in a math class that have a cat.
This number is best considered as a [_]{$rational}{5}.
END_PGML
############################################################ # Solution ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION This proportion will be a ratio of integers, as both the total number of people in the class and the number of people who have a cat are integers. So the rational numbers are the appropriate set.
END_PGML_SOLUTION
Section::End();
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML The number of people in the room with you who have the same birthday as you.
This number is best considered as a [_]{$natural}{5}.
END_PGML
############################################################ # Solution ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION We know that the number of people must be a counting number, and since _you_ are in the room with yourself, there is at least one person in that room with your birthday. So the natural numbers are the appropriate set.
END_PGML_SOLUTION
Section::End();
############################################################ # Section ############################################################ Section::Begin("");
BEGIN_PGML The total revenue (in dollars) generated for ticket sales at a Timbers soccer game.
This number is best considered as a [_]{$rational}{5}.
END_PGML
############################################################ # Solution ############################################################
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION The total revenue will be some number of dollars and cents, such as [`\$631{,}897.15\text{,}`] which is a terminating decimal and thus a rational number. So the rational numbers are the appropriate set.
END_PGML_SOLUTION
Section::End();
Scaffold::End();
